well stuck in the emergency room hallway  that's what one local woman's ordeal  over at mountain view hospital mary jane  belliesa shares this patient's request  for answers and why covet may be to  blame  siobhan young says she arrived to  mountain view hospital sunday night due  to an infection in her leg since then  she's been waiting in the emergency room  hallway for a room and has yet to be  seen by a doctor  it's going on 30 40 hours and i'm in the  hallway i have no medication  they haven't i'm diabetic so my sugar  hasn't been checked  and i'm just i'm just here nobody's  telling me anything what's going on  young says it's hard to even ask for  assistance she says another patient  helped her use the restroom  i'm trying to get up to use the bathroom  i'm really weak i can barely walk  and the doctors and nurses are just  standing around and they just  watching me struggle basically dr  dominic martinello the chief medical  officer at mountain view medical center  says the pandemic has pushed hospitals  to their capacity creating a backlog of  patients with these big spikes and a lot  of people showing up and then right  after that all the deferred care starts  coming in so the people who were unable  to get treated in a timely manner young  says as much as she'd like to go to  another hospital she's unable to drive  or find other means of transportation i  feel like i'm forgot about honestly i  feel like i'm just thrown in a corner  and they completely forgot about me  we're hiring new people every day we're  getting creative with the way that we do  our jobs and we're putting in that  hundred and ten percent because at the  end of the day you know we want to take  care of ourselves but we also  desperately want to take care of these  patients mountain view hospital will be  expanding their emergency room this  includes adding in more beds dr  martinello says this expansion will  allow more staff to see more patients  faster reporting from cheyenne antinea